From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 12:32:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] renderer: run copies for wrapped textures, GL-thread timing,
 fractional display scale

- A texture that is not one run of host memory (the movie picture that wraps past the end
  of VRAM) is copied run by run with GuestMemory::copy_out instead of byte by byte (80 ms
  per MB on the Vita's CPU, every movie frame).
- settings.timing=N (INFECTED_GL_TIMING): a [gl-time] line every N presents with target
  switches, the first draw after each switch, other draws, texture uploads and the swap;
  gpu_timing=1 adds a glFinish before the swap and reports its wait.
- settings.display_scale_percent (INFECTED_GL_DISPLAY_SCALE_PERCENT, 100..300): display
  targets drawn at that percentage of 480x272 (150 = 720x408) and enlarged to the window
  with the blit's linear filter. Target::scale is a float; viewport, scissor and read-back
  already scaled by a factor. Desktop replay of flips 4200-4203 at 150 checked by eye.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

